WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:07.860
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.830
Episode 9

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.830
「High School Astronomy Network」

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.660
Just one word is fine.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.540
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.630
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.760
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.880
Your answers will...

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.850
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.300
Even more...

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.180
Like fireworks...

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:46.400
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:53.400
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.910
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:05.080
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:11.050
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:19.260
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:24.520
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:36.030
Since we have quite a few people today, let's review.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.400
Oumi Ayumi (Nogishiro President)

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.020
Sakuragawa (Vice President) and Musa (the hottie)

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.480
Maibara (nickname: "Mochi-mochi")

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.030
Kawamura & Minami (Takami Girls' School)

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.490
You look excited, President Oumi.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.910
You think?

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:47.500
I'm going upstairs.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:48.880
Take care of the rest, will you?

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.050
Oh, stop shortening your skirt, okay?

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.340
President!

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.980
Saku-chan! Hurry up! Hurry up!

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.730
The rest of you, hurry up too! Hurry up!

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.240
Mihoshi! Look, you need to put this on.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.700
You think she'll run inside the train too?

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:28.370
But I'm really happy that an exciting network such as the Prefectural High School Astronomy Network invited us.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.210
I'll be stargazing with people other than those from our school.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.790
It'll be my first time!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.510
I still remember the exchanges we had with other universities.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:41.220
I wasn't interested in astronomy back when I was in high school, so this will be my first time too.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.350
Huh? What's wrong?

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:44.890
They're definitely...

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:48.270
I think they must be hardcore stargazers.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:49.190
"Hardcore stargazers"?

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.940
Wah! I'm so excited!

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.320
Undefeated in 400 matches !

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.820
I wonder what they're like?

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.440
Hmph... The real question is,

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:00.450
what grade is Oumi-san in?!

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.700
That?!

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.200
I'm not really looking forward to anything in particular...

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.370
Instead, I just hope that no more love rivals appear.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:16.800
Although, I've only worked with people from outside our school
through the astronomy group in the Science Club I used to belong to,

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.170
I'm sure they're nice people.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:23.760
After all, people who love stars are wonderful people-

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.430
It's beautiful!

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.980
It's on a completely different scale than our little private school, isn't it?

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.600
Um... Where are we supposed to go?

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.610
Hello!

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.860
I'll be...

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:39.690
...right there!

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.870
Sorry to keep you all waiting-

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.090
I'm the President of Nogishiro High School's Astronomy Club, Oumi Ayumi, a third year.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.050
I'm honored that you could come.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.840
No, the honor is ours. This is our first time meeting.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.130
I'm the President, Roma-

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.300
The first time?

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.430
Really? Is it really the first time?

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:10.560
Oumi!

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.520
Are they from Souei High School?

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:16.690
Hello.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.480
I'm the Vice President, Sakuragawa.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:20.940
I'm Musa, a sophomore.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:21.860
I'm Miyamae.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.030
I'm Yahata.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.240
I'm Youkaichi.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:25.490
I'm Ichinobe.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:26.620
I'm Miyako.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.530
E-Eight?

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:29.580
There are eight of you?!

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.410
No, there are a few more upstairs.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.960
T-There are more?!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.630
Now then, please follow me. The roof is this way.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.640
Hello.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:50.720
Hello.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:51.680
Hello.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.230
Hello.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:54.690
Everyone,

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.810
please come inside.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.370
This is our club's 20cm refracting telescope.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.920
Am... Am I dreaming?

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.920
To see something like this in a school...

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:24.760
If we take just the diameter, it's the same length as the telescope at Haruko-san's place!

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:28.010
Oh, it's only worth a few cars.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.800
And exactly how much is that?!

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.770
President, the other schools have also arrived.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.820
The atmospheric scintillation appears to be poor.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.280
Yeah, despite the weather looking fairly good...

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.570
What type of lens does your SLR camera use?

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.570
35mm F/1.8 fixed lens.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.080
I've got a fetish for Perseus.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.540
All right! Tonight, I'm gonna talk!

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.710
H-Hardcore stargazers...

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.300
Behave, Mihoshi! We still don't know who they are.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:03.920
President!

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.970
Are you from Souei High School?

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:08.680
Nice to meet you.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.510
I'm Kawamura from Takami All Girls' High School.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:11.640
I'm Minami.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.970
You guys travel light, don't you?

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:14.850
Well, yeah...

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:15.980
Very!

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:20.350
Listen, Mihoshi, don't get too excited, okay?

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:21.060
Okay.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.110
There. I've written it on your hand.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.940
Don't get too
excited

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.110
Everyone's looking this way.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.910
It's because you're all so cute.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.580
By the way, which constellation do you have a fetish for?

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.750
Spill it! Spill it!

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:42.000
When we step outside, we're faced with reality.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.130
Our sole piece of equipment.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.380
Oh dear, equipment troubles?

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:49.010
Well, that's easy then.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.760
We'll just have to get along.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.680
W-We just have... to get along?

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.890
It's exactly as I said.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.730
After all, equipment wise, we have no problems at all.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.610
Oh, my. I see you've made friends already.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.280
By the looks of it, it won't be a problem even if we do divide you into groups.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.360
Divide us... into groups?

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:12.070
Yup.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.660
There are more of us now,

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.740
so it'll help you get to know us faster.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.580
Although, we will start with free stargazing first.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.170
Let's wait for the moon to set, so we can measure the night's darkness.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.830
Darkness?!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:28.090
The program for today is printed, so please refer to this.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.720
Oh? So, your name's Hime?

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.840
Cute girls have cute names too.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.430
Let's make this an enjoyable night!

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:50.150
Somehow, it feels like we're at a festival.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.070
Look! Look! They're displaying star maps on a laptop!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:54.490
It's so hi-tech!

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:57.990
Wah! I want to look at everyone's.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.120
Please go ahead.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.170
Don't get too
excited

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.630
I'm telling you!

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.000
You're too carefree!

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.220
They asked us to divide into groups, so we're already separated!

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.680
Edogawa?

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.760
S-Sabato...

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.220
I see Sabato Kuroi...

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.730
How am I supposed to fight this?!

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.230
Is something wrong?

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.650
Although it's still early, please make your way to your assigned groups.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.570
We'll be starting our explanations.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.030
Now then, Makita-san, come with me.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.990
Yaraicchi, over here. This way!

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.200
Akeno-san, you're with me!

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:40.700
Now then, Edogawa-kun...

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:42.910
Let's work hard together since we're all freshmen.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.210
No!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.420
Will they be okay?

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.420
Um, where should the President and I go?

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.260
You two are with us.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:09:00.890
Now then, let the periodic Prefectural High School Astronomy Network's stargazing session begin!

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:07.480
Now then, I will explain how we'll be stargazing.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:12.320
Tonight's theme is measuring the darkness of the night.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.490
I'm sure that you're all familiar with it through making meteor observations.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:16.950
Yes, we are!

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:16.910
Yes, we are!

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.120
You are?!

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:25.330
What we'll use for the calculation will be our eyes, the stars that spread far out above us, and the Area Method.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:30.500
We'll count the number of stars we observe within a certain area,

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:35.970
and use that to determine the magnitude of the faintest star.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.220
During Fall, the area within the Great Square of Pegasus is normally used.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.180
Tonight, we will count the number of stars that lie within that area.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:49.560
Using our results, we'll be able to calculate the extent of the light pollution in this area,

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.780
and I believe this will benefit us greatly in our future activities.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.940
Although, it's a really boring thing to do.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:03.240
But I'm convinced that the time we spend together will benefit us all greatly.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.330
Tonight, Souei High School will be joining us.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:14.260
We'll take an average of all counts done by each group, so all groups, please do your best.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:21.140
Well then, please stargaze freely until the moon sets at 21:05.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.140
And with that, lights off!

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:27.730
Let's go!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:28.730
All right, let's go!

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.600
Astronomy Photography Boys!

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:31.310
Go!

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:32.770
No!

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.820
Souei High School!

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.030
I've focused it on the moon; please come up here to take a look.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.910
It's your first time, so we're giving you priority.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.410
It's a half moon tonight, so you'll be able to see the craters clearly.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.040
Moon? Craters?!

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:49.750
Of course.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.460
Yaha-chan.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:55.800
I feel like a big sister for the first time in my life.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.510
Yes, but she's a sophomore.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.720
We can see the other side of the moon compared to when we did our moon viewing.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.600
I really wanted to show you the moon.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.940
So that's why you didn't schedule the stargazing session on a new moon, right?

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:15.650
And if the moon rises after 9 o'clock, it shouldn't affect our stargazing either.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:16.190
Yes.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:20.490
And there aren't any other views which make me more proud than this one.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.620
Fully equipped and in a safe location.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.410
It's all thanks to the High School Astronomy Network that we're blessed with the resources to be active.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.830
Or maybe it's all thanks to Oumi-san.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:33.210
No way. This wouldn't have been possible if no one attended.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.880
Oh, my. Don't be so modest.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:34.790
Oh, my. Don't be so modest.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.960
Look! We can still see the Summer Triangle.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.260
You're right.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.590
The dark space that's approaching from behind it,

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.220
that must be the autumn sky.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.230
It's as though a dark hole has appeared in the sky.

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:53.190
But Oumi likes the autumn sky best.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:53.690
What?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.520
Rather, what's that rising from the east right this moment?

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.530
Northeast.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.280
Let's see. Let me just load this up.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.240
It's Capella from the Aurigae constellation.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.240
[Note: The Aurigae constellation's shape has been associated with the pointed helmet of a charioteer. Cappella is its brightest star.]

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.530
When Fomalhaut is around here...

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.530
[Note: Fomalhaut is the brightest star in the Piscis Austrinus constellation.]

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:09.500
...and Deneb Kaitos is around here,

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:09.540
[Note: Deneb Kaitos, also termed Beta Ceti, is the brightest star in the Cetus constellation.]

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:11.870
then Capella is found here.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.250
This girl... she's really useful!

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.040
Then, what about that?

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.500
The tip of the Grus constellation!

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.550
Then, what about that one?

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.260
A black space!

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.340
The wind's picking up.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.510
What? I'll wonder if we'll be okay...

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.760
Oh, can I borrow your radio?

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.270
I see. I see.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.850
It appears that a few clouds have developed,

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:35.560
but because there's a wind, the clouds should just pass by.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:38.230
Rather...

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.690
...it's the first time I've seen someone...

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.190
...actually draw out a weather map.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.860
Why, Souei-san, you're good.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.910
Well, we're just very low-tech.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.120
Great! Keep it up!

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.000
Place your target in the center and release!

00:12:58.380 --> 00:12:59.210
Ooyagi-kun,

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:02.260
do you have a moment?

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.640
It's cold.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.430
It's getting chilly.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.020
Makita-san, are you all right?

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.100
Aren't you cold?

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.690
N-No, this is my policy.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.690
W-What are you laughing at?

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.650
It's nothing. Honestly.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.860
I just thought that you're really cute.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.320
I-I hate people who say things like that so soon.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.070
Your boyfriend doesn't tell you that?

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.530
What?! I don't have a boyfriend.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:32.790
Oh? Then you're single.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.790
What's it to you?!

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.340
It's what gentlemen do when they see a lady looking cold.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:43.510
You can thank me with a date.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.880
I-I don't need a coat!

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.810
Hey, you over there! Go back to the roof.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:52.390
Oh, shit!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.270
We're sorry.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.220
We're sorry.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:56.560
I wondered what it was.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:57.940
So, it was patrolling, eh?

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.690
I'm sorry for taking you out of the session.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.650
I honestly don't want to be so strict,

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:06.740
but if anything happens, it'll affect the stargazing session and the High School Astronomy Network.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.740
So we need to be careful of these kinds of situations when there are a lot of people present, right?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:12.490
You're amazing.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.700
Please stop that. You're embarrassing me.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:20.330
Tonight, Souei High School's really working hard, so I want to make this a good session.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.170
Look, it's Fomalhaut.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:24.550
Autumn's sole star.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.630
This year, we haven't had any planets, so it's kind of sad.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:33.850
I get the feeling that another year's passed when I see this view.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.430
Every single year.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.440
I hear that you like the autumn stars.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:40.690
My president-

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:40.690
Well,

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.530
we've patrolled the whole area, so let's head back.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.280
The moon's setting soon.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.540
You needn't have gone to the extent of following me to return it.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.370
I've already got someone I like.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:00.710
I'm heading back to the roof.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.040
Wait!

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:10.720
Great, Edogawa-kun. Keep it up!

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.930
Let's go! Our astronomy photography!

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:16.680
That was... Hime-chan's voice...

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:20.190
Who was that?!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:20.890
What happened-

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.950
You're mean, Hime-chan.

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:40.540
I'm sorry!

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.580
I didn't realize it was like that.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.290
I'm heading back to the roof.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.210
Wait!

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.010
Musa's view + Musa's impression

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:00.230
I'm sorry.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.190
I-I was convinced that...

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.940
You don't need to apologize.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:06.110
It's Musa-kun's fault to begin with.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.150
I didn't do anything.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:09.990
I'm offended.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:13.410
Oh, really? You're supposed to be on the roof still.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:19.370
You've been with us for a long time now and you're enthusiastic about our activities, so I trust you.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:20.750
Don't betray my trust.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:23.460
I want you to trust me.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:28.670
I-I didn't know how to react to something like this.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:33.550
Are you all right?

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.890
For now, let's head back to the roof.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:37.760
O-Ooyagi-kun?

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.560
Ooyagi-kun...

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:41.390
Ooyagi-kun!

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:43.810
You're mean, Hime-chan.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.810
You rejected mine when I lent it to you.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.940
Could it be that the person you mentioned liking earlier is-

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.660
There they are!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:56.740
President!

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.660
The moon's set.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:01.200
What were you doing?

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.000
Oumi, did something happen?

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:04.540
It's nothing.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:05.370
We'll be right there.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.420
Well then, let's go.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:08.790
But...

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.420
It looks like Makita-san's calmed down now.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.760
Saku-chan! Hime-chan!

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.300
Thank goodness. We looked all over for you.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.050
The stargazing session's starting.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.430
It's the main event!

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.600
You shouldn't leave the roof unless you need to use the toilet.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.600
Mid-air! Mid-air!

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.770
Hime-chan, what's wrong? Are you cold?

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:29.150
I-I-I-It's nothing.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:38.410
It's much darker now that the moon has set.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.410
Every group has a record chart, correct?

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:47.370
Then let's start calculating the night's darkness.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:50.380
Hoshimi-chan, over here. Over here!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:51.420
Hoshimi-chan?

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:54.010
This group wants you to look at the stars.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:54.800
Okay!

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:57.840
Ooyagi-kun.

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:01.470
Thank you for changing the topic.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.470
It's just a blanket, but please use it.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:08.150
You said yourself that you wanted to make this a good stargazing session.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:13.610
To be honest, not all Nogishiro students here are club members.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:14.030
What?

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:19.320
Most of them are event members who only participate in outings and stargazing sessions.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.830
For example, Musa-kun belongs to the Light Music Club.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.490
We only have nine official members.

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:27.040
I-I see.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:27.870
Yes...

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:29.370
I was convinced that...

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.210
I didn't mean to lie to you.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.300
But because everyone was saying that we're amazing, it started to get fun.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:37.970
I'm sorry.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:39.970
Maybe I wanted to show off.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:44.970
Is it strange for me to invite non-official members as well as other schools?

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.020
N-No, it's not.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:48.890
But why?

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.650
Because I want everyone to see.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:57.940
There are very few people who will go and buy a telescope to watch the stars even if they're interested.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:02.160
But there are many who will see them if they can do so freely.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:06.160
Luckily, we have that freedom.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.410
And that's why, I want everyone to see them.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.080
That's all.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.800
It's the same for Souei High School.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:19.340
Our wishes were the same from the very beginning.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:20.760
Didn't I already say so?

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:23.470
All we have to do is get along.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:29.730
That's how I repay the person who taught me how to stargaze.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:33.860
Roma-kun,

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:41.450
after we've calculated the darkness, can you talk about the legends?

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.280
It'll be my pleasure.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:55.590
To look for constellations during the Fall, we should start by looking for the Great Square of Pegasus.

00:19:56.420 --> 00:20:01.880
But during Fall, it's nice to follow its characters in order.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.720
Cepheus, the ancient Aethiopian king,

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.680
and his queen, Cassiopeia.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:14.350
Her continual bragging about her daughter, Andromeda, angered the sea god, Poseidon,

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.520
so Andromeda was sacrificed to the sea.

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.370
Just when she was about to be engulfed by the sea monster,

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:31.910
the hero Perseus, riding on Pegasus, rescued her.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:43.930
Andromeda was saved by Perseus.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:48.350
The two fell in love and lived happily ever after.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:53.100
Amazing!

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.150
The characters are lined up one after another.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.560
[Note: An emakimono is a horizontal illustrative scroll that combines both text and pictures. It's the origin of manga.]

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:56.560
It's like an emakimono!

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:58.940
It's the same area we were just looking at...

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:02.940
I hadn't realized the area surrounding the observation area was so cool!

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.950
Fetish... fetish for Perseus.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.530
Please call me your Andromeda.

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:12.620
Sakuragawa, adjust the focus to M52.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:13.210
Sure.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.750
President, let's watch too.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:20.090
Yes, let's watch what we can.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:22.090
We want to watch this with someone.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:23.760
We want to be able to see far away.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:28.390
We all look up at the sky with various emotions in our heart.

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:30.140
What we want to see;

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:31.520
what we want others to see...

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.810
our emotions in our heart.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:48.160
Our gaze... has reached the universe.

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:55.330
Was that so?

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:57.170
You were at Goshima Science Museum?

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.880
Yes, we belonged to the same Astronomy Club.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:03.460
We became friends, but you suddenly quit.

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:05.630
I was worried about you.

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:10.180
Oh, to be honest, it was because my body couldn't handle the commute.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:11.180
I see.

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:15.730
I was sad when I spotted you during the Fall when we were freshmen.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:17.850
You just sat quietly at the reception.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:19.900
If I remember correctly, there were so many people, it made me feel sick.

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.230
But I'm happy that we were able to hold a good stargazing session this year.

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:38.000
Though I did wonder what I should do if you didn't remember me.

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:44.090
It was a fun stargazing session thanks to you, Hoshimi-chan.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:46.050
Every household needs one.

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:49.430
But now we've got to focus all our efforts on our entrance exams.

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:51.140
Us poor seniors...

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:52.350
Seniors...

00:22:52.550 --> 00:22:53.430
Entrance exams...

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:56.270
P-P-P-President, have you prepared?

00:22:56.470 --> 00:22:57.730
O-Of course-

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:02.400
I'm still a sophomore, so see you again, Hime-chan.

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:03.820
I don't want to see you again!

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:06.190
Besides, apparently, you're not even a member!

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:11.320
We'll be responsible for calculating the total.

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:12.620
It's a shame though.

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:17.330
It became cloudy near dawn, so we couldn't show you Saturn.

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:19.120
Saturn, eh?

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:21.920
What's that? You want a telescope now?

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:23.040
Yeah.

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:26.760
You may come use ours at any time.

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:28.920
Everyone...

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:30.880
Place your target in the center and release...

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:33.050
Girl photos!

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:35.100
Let me take them!

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:37.560
Girl photos!

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:37.890
Calm down!

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:38.730
The bus is here.

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:39.390
Hop on!

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:40.940
No!

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:42.770
Let's stargaze together again sometime.

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:56.870
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:00.540
but I can’t find the words,

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:03.880
I want to tell you,

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:06.380
but they just slip away…

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:10.050
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:14.640
In this Wave of Silence,

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:19.020
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:24.310
playing with my memories

00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:30.150
and releasing my heart.

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:33.070
Into the future,

00:24:33.070 --> 00:24:41.660
I will have these feelings again!

00:24:42.080 --> 00:24:46.080
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:24:46.330 --> 00:24:51.170
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:24:51.170 --> 00:25:00.060
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:04.230
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:10.480
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:25:15.030 --> 00:25:20.040
Next time: Together

00:25:15.610 --> 00:25:17.410
Next time, on Sora no Manimani:

00:25:17.700 --> 00:25:18.370
Together.

00:25:18.870 --> 00:25:19.830
Let's go watch the stars together.

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:25.040
Mihoshi (11th Grade) and Souma Nozomu (Age 30 and single)

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:25.040
go out together on a weekend.

00:25:25.040 --> 00:25:30.040
The curious bunch becomes detectives?

00:25:25.040 --> 00:25:30.040
What exactly did they see...?
